A Minor Project that predicts stock prices using Linear Regression and real-time market data from Yahoo Finance.

 Overview

StockSight is a simple full-stack web application that:

Fetches real-time stock data
Trains a Linear Regression model
Predicts future stock prices
Displays results using interactive charts

This project is designed to demonstrate ML + Web Integration in a beginner-friendly way.

🗂 Project Structure
stock-predictor/
├── backend/
│   ├── app.py             
│   └── requirements.txt    
└── frontend/
    └── index.html    

⚙️ Tech Stack
Layer	Technology
Frontend	HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Chart.js
Backend	Python, Flask, Flask-CORS
ML Model	scikit-learn (Linear Regression)
Data Source	yfinance (Yahoo Finance API)


🚀 Features
📊 Real-time stock data fetching
🤖 Machine Learning-based price prediction
📈 Interactive charts using Chart.js
🌐 Simple and lightweight frontend
⚡ Fast API built with Flask

🛠️ Setup & Run
Step 1 — Backend Setup
cd backend

# Create virtual environment (recommended)
python -m venv venv

# Activate environment
source venv/bin/activate       # Mac/Linux
venv\Scripts\activate          # Windows

# Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# Run the Flask server
python app.py

✅ Backend will run at:
👉 http://localhost:5000

Step 2 — Frontend

Simply open the file in your browser:

frontend/index.html

You can:

Double-click the file
OR drag and drop into your browser
🔮 How It Works
User enters a stock symbol (e.g., AAPL, TSLA)
Backend fetches historical data using yfinance
Data is preprocessed using MinMaxScaler
A Linear Regression model is trained
Predictions are generated
Results are sent to frontend
Chart.js displays actual vs predicted prices